      "aboutMarkdown": "### What it is\n\nOmarchy is a Linux distribution with a preconfigured desktop and a strong set of defaults. It is built for people who want to use, understand, and customize their computer.\n\n### Link\n\n- [Omarchy](https://omarchy.org/)",
      "personalInterestDate": "2025-07-01",
      "personalInterestLabel": "Started caring, July 2025",
      "markerLabel": "discovered",
      "contextMarkdown": "### The Windows-to-Linux jump\n\nFor years I was tired of Windows performance issues and interested in Linux, but I kept postponing the switch. Gaming was part of the reason: when I still played games such as League of Legends, Linux felt like a compromise.\n\nAfter some laptop problems, and once gaming mattered less, I installed Linux to see if it could help. In July 2025, while hiking in Asturias, I watched DHH’s interview with Lex Fridman. The ambition and positivity behind Omarchy clicked immediately.\n\nIt changed how I use my computer. I love understanding how computers work, customizing them, and treating the machine as something to explore. The idea of a computer for people who love computers felt like a description of me.",
