      "sourceUrl": "https://trends.google.com/explore?q=AI&date=today%205-y&geo=Worldwide",
      "aboutMarkdown": "### What it is\n\nArtificial intelligence is the field of building systems that perform tasks linked with human intelligence, such as learning, perception, language, and reasoning. This chart follows the broad search term AI, not one product.\n\n### Link\n\n- [Artificial intelligence](https://www.britannica.com/technology/artificial-intelligence)",
      "personalInterestDate": "2021-11-01",
      "personalInterestLabel": "Discovered, Nov 2021",
      "markerLabel": "discovered",
      "contextMarkdown": "### From autocomplete to ChatGPT\n\nI was always interested in coding, but I started with the normal tools: Stack Overflow, documentation, and a lot of trial and error.\n\nIn November 2021, while writing my master’s thesis, an early GPT-style autocomplete tool appeared. It was not a chat interface yet, but the idea of software completing code felt important.\n\nChatGPT in November 2022 was the real break. I became obsessed with asking it questions, using it at work, exploring coding tools such as [v0](https://v0.dev), and talking about it with everyone.\n\nI kept watching the conversation move through YouTube and Hacker News. The shift felt different from the skepticism around crypto: people I respected began treating AI as a real change in how software and knowledge work could happen.",
