      "aboutMarkdown": "### What it is\n\nTesla is a company that makes electric vehicles, battery storage, solar products, and related software. Search interest can reflect both its products and public attention around the company.\n\n### Link\n\n- [Tesla](https://www.tesla.com/)",
      "personalInterestDate": "2019-11-01",
      "personalInterestLabel": "Started investing, Nov 2019",
      "markerLabel": "invested",
      "contextMarkdown": "### From curiosity to conviction\n\nI was aware of Tesla around 2013, when friends and I talked about the Model S, electric cars, and what the future of transport might look like. I was interested in the engineering before I became interested in the stock.\n\nThe turning point was the Cybertruck announcement. I started finding YouTube videos that explained it from an engineering perspective, and I became obsessed with the company, its business model, its technology, and how it might affect the world.\n\nI think I started investing in November 2019, roughly a month before the stock began its extraordinary run. The chart marker is set to November 2019 for now: it marks the investing chapter, while the personal story starts earlier.\n\nThat interest eventually became my master’s thesis: [Tesla’s Robotaxi network](\/documents\/Tesla%20Robotaxi%20-%20Master%20Thesis.pdf), a quantitative analysis of adoption, economic impact, and implications.",
